<title>RUSSIA: Russia wants energy minister to head utility board.</title>
<headline>Russia wants energy minister to head utility board.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian government has recommended Fuel and Energy Minister Pyotr Rodionov also serve as chairman of the board at national power utility UES, cabinet spokesman Igor Shabdurasulov told a news conference on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Rodionov, appointed minister last year, was once head of a St Petersburg subsidiary of national gas monopoly RAO Gazprom.</p>
<p>Gazprom said last week that it wanted to buy a 25 percent stake in Unified Energy System, or UES.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
